        {
            "number": 4,
            "revision": "cf7c959cc3ce1512ab52957fb6aa88ca8810b280",
            "parents": [
                "6caa1d164475eeacb524290accd346a3002828a3"
            ],
            "ref": "refs/changes/28/89528/4",
            "uploader": {
                "name": "JY-Voon",
                "email": "jvoon@nvidia.com",
                "username": "JY-Voon"
            },
            "createdOn": 1777540785,
            "author": {
                "name": "Ender",
                "email": "andhsieh@nvidia.com",
                "username": "Ender-Hsieh"
            },
            "kind": "TRIVIAL_REBASE_WITH_MESSAGE_UPDATE",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Marc Olberding",
                        "email": "molberding@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "molbear"
                    },
                    "message": "coroutines in our testing reduced performance by up to 50%, a minimum of 30% please do not introduce coroutines here."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "We will never support boost::coroutines in this repo.  We never should've supported them in sdbusplus in the first place.\n\nCertainly we will not be enabling them in nvidia-gpu, as they cause performance and maintenance issues."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ender",
                        "email": "andhsieh@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "Ender-Hsieh"
                    },
                    "message": "Hi @ed@tanous.net, @molberding@nvidia.com,\n\nThanks for the clear feedback. We will abandon this patch.\n\nI now understand the perf cost of boost::coroutines and agree it's the wrong tool here.\n\nFor our Reset use case, the operation typically completes within a few seconds, and we want the caller to receive 200 only after the response is available.\n\nBesides @jvoon@nvidia.com's proposed sdbusplus deferred-reply API, would the pattern used in certificate_service.hpp's GenerateCSR also be an option?\n\nThere, the daemon kicks off the work and returns the D-Bus reply immediately, while bmcweb keeps the HTTP request open by holding AsyncResp inside both a D-Bus signal subscription and a timeout. \nWhen the daemon finishes and emits the completion signal, bmcweb's signal callback fills in the response and sends 200 to the caller; if the timeout fires first, an error is returned instead."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ender",
                        "email": "andhsieh@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "Ender-Hsieh"
                    },
                    "message": "Got it. Thanks"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/nvidia-gpu/MctpRequester.cpp",
                    "line": 271,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Marc Olberding",
                        "email": "molberding@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "molbear"
                    },
                    "message": "no, stackfull coroutines are broken. Do not do this. Stackless coroutine support severely pessimizes performance, due to all sorts of inneffecencies in the implementation. This was previously nonblocking without coroutines and without any allocations in the hotpath, please do not add overhead in the hotpath."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/nvidia-gpu/MctpRequester.cpp",
                    "line": 271,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ender",
                        "email": "andhsieh@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "Ender-Hsieh"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged. Thank you for your reply."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/nvidia-gpu/MctpRequester.hpp",
                    "line": 59,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Marc Olberding",
                        "email": "molberding@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "molbear"
                    },
                    "message": "you are forcing an alloc here where there wasn't before in the hotpath, don't alloc in the hotpath."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/nvidia-gpu/MctpRequester.hpp",
                    "line": 59,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ender",
                        "email": "andhsieh@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "Ender-Hsieh"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged. Thank you for your reply."
                }
            ],
